<GuideLayout 
  title="Global Activewear Logistics: Tax & Duty Optimization"
  description="Navigate the complexities of international trade and learn how to optimize your supply chain for better margins."
  publishDate="June 26, 2026"
>
  <p>For B2B activewear buyers, the price on the invoice is only half the story. The total landed cost—including freight, duties, and taxes—determines your true profit margin. Our logistics team works daily with global brands to optimize this process.</p>

  <h2>1. Understanding Harmonized System (HS) Codes</h2>
  <p>Misclassifying activewear can lead to massive overpayments in duty. Our shipping experts ensure every shipment of yoga sets or sports bras is classified correctly to take advantage of the lowest possible duty rates under your country's specific trade agreements.</p>

  <h2>2. Direct-to-Consumer (D2C) Bulk Shipping</h2>
  <p>We offer specialized logistics solutions for brands that sell globally. By strategically splitting shipments or utilizing bonded warehouses, we help our clients minimize the tax burden of importing large volumes while maintaining fast delivery times to their end customers.</p>

</GuideLayout>
